      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now let me check the compile script and some helper classes to understand the full API.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several issues reducing understandability:\n1. Dead code: unused helper methods (`assertFailedIndexExtractorConstructor`, `assertIndexExtractorMerge`, `testCardinalityAndIsEmpty`, `testCopy`)\n2. Invalid/broken Java: `private T __super_createEmptyFilter(Shape shape);` uses undefined generic `T` and has no body\n3. `createFilter` methods also use undefined generic `T`\n4. Long single-line expressions for `BitMapExtractor` creation\n5. No structure within `testContains` to explain which aspect is being tested\n\nLet me write the improved version.Now let me compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully (`COMPILE_OK`)."
